In a bid to automate backup processes, the xFusionCorp Industries sysadmin team has developed a new bash script named xfusioncorp.sh. 
While the script has been distributed to all necessary servers, it lacks executable permissions on App Server 3 within the Stratos Datacenter.

Your task is to grant executable permissions to the /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh script on App Server 3. Additionally, ensure that all users have the capability to execute it.

SOLUTION
Steps to Complete the Task
1. SSH into App Server 3
bash
ssh username@app-server-3
# Or use the specific hostname/IP provided in your environment
2. Verify the script exists
bash
ls -l /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
You'll likely see something like:

text
-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1234 Oct  8 10:30 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
Notice there are no x (execute) permissions yet.

3. Grant executable permissions to ALL users
Use chmod with the a+x flag (where a = all users: owner, group, others):

bash
sudo chmod a+x /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
Alternative equivalent commands:

bash
# Using symbolic mode
sudo chmod +x /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh

# Using octal mode (adds execute to rw-r--r-- → rwxr-xr-x)
sudo chmod 755 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
💡 Note: chmod +x (without specifying who) applies execute permission to all users by default (subject to umask), so it achieves the same result as a+x.

4. Verify the permissions
bash
ls -l /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
Expected output:

text
-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 1234 Oct  8 10:30 /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
The x in positions for owner, group, and others confirms all users can execute the script. ✅

✅ One-Liner Solution
bash
sudo chmod +x /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
🔍 Optional: Test the Script
To confirm it actually executes:

bash
/tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
# Or
bash /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh
📝 Quick Reference: Permission Modes
Mode	Symbolic	Meaning
755	rwxr-xr-x	Owner: rwx, Group: r-x, Others: r-x
+x	adds x to all	Everyone can execute
a+x	adds x to all	Explicitly everyone can execute
u+x	adds x to owner only	Only owner can execute
o+x	adds x to others only	Only others can execute
The task is complete once /tmp/xfusioncorp.sh shows -rwxr-xr-x (or any permission set where all three user classes have the x bit set).

